NVEL scaling and segmentation provenance
========================================

Version 0.1.0 independently ports the `NUMLOG`, `SEGMNT`, `SCRIB`, and
`INTL14` routines from the US Forest Service National Volume Estimator Library
at commit 38548071d5aa652bb90c7f111f86b427f798a1c9. The upstream files read
were `numlog.f`, `segmnt.f`, and `scrib.f`.

The `numlog.f` and `segmnt.f` headers carry this authorship credit:

    THE LOGIC WAS DEVELOPED BY JIM BRICKELL, TCFPM R-1, AND
    IMPLEMENTED BY WO-TM.

This is an authorship credit, not a copyright notice. No additional copyright
holder is inferred from it. The reviewed headers of `scrib.f`, including the
`INTL14` routine in that file, contain no copyright or authorship notice.

The source repository, pinned revision, files, and date read are recorded in
`inst/NOTES.md`. Later discoveries must be added rather than silently dropped.


