Authorship credits recorded as provenance (maintainer decision, 2026-09-06)
===================================================================

The following authorship credits appear in the library's source comments. They
are not copyright notices. They are preserved so each ported equation set has
an auditable lineage. No additional copyright holder is inferred from them.
All citations refer to upstream commit
38548071d5aa652bb90c7f111f86b427f798a1c9.

- `profile.f`, lines 8 through 11, credits taper or profile models developed by
  Jim Flewelling, Ray Czaplewski, Wensel and Olson, and John Byrne, and credits
  the Forest Management Service Center for merchandising logic.
- `f_other.f`, lines 175 through 177, credits additions to K. Cormier and the
  original code to J. W. Flewelling.
- `r1tap.f`, lines 22 through 23, credits the primary profile coefficients to
  John Byrne. Line 109 credits the other-species coefficients to Chojnacky and
  Cutler.
- `r4d2h.f`, line 7, credits the equation to David Chojnacky and Research Paper
  INT-339.
- `r10d2h.f`, lines 5 and 16 through 19, credits equations or references to
  Larsen and Winterberger, Larson and coauthors, Haack, Gregory and coauthors,
  Brackett, and Malone and coauthors. It also records a modification by Y. Wang.
- `r10volo.f`, line 9, names D. DeMars and M. Schmidt as authors and K. Cormier
  and B. Jones as converters.
- `r8vol2.f`, line 26, names Ken Cormier and Brad Jones as authors.
- `r9coeff.inc`, lines 4 through 9, identifies the Clark and others 1991
  profile equations in Research Paper SE-282 and records Mike VanDyck's 2013
  yellow birch coefficient refit.
- `r5tap.f`, lines 14 and 35, identifies the Wensel and Krumland profile model.
- `r12tap.f`, line 5, identifies the Hawaii profile as the Sharpneck model.
- `blmtap.f` identifies its coefficient system as Behre's hyperbola.
  The following credit lines are transcribed verbatim from commit
  38548071d5aa652bb90c7f111f86b427f798a1c9:

  Line 93:

      C     Jim Alegria, OSO 930.

  Line 101:

      C--  using an iterative method devised by Jim Alegria, September, 1993.

  Line 218:

      C      20 Sep 93; R. Miller, OSO 931.5
- `stump.f`, lines 1 through 3, records creation by Y. Wang and a Raile 1982
  equation. Line 177 credits Raile for the integration formula.

The inventory includes the BLMTAP credits added under the standing maintainer
